WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.240
- Today, we're celebrating
a Drew Gooder right here,

00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:06.290
and she's from Watts, South Los Angeles,

00:00:06.290 --> 00:00:09.260
and has spent the last 50
years educating children

00:00:09.260 --> 00:00:11.310
from underserved communities.

00:00:11.310 --> 00:00:12.613
Take a look at her story.

00:00:13.550 --> 00:00:17.890
- Hi, I'm Dolores Sheen, aka Aunt Dolores.

00:00:17.890 --> 00:00:20.660
And I'm the executive
director and co-founder

00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:22.690
of the Sheenway School and Culture Center

00:00:22.690 --> 00:00:24.400
in Watts South LA.

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:27.170
The school opened in 1971,

00:00:27.170 --> 00:00:28.690
50 years ago,

00:00:28.690 --> 00:00:32.480
and we're still here
reaching and teaching.

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:33.670
I was going to be a doctor.

00:00:33.670 --> 00:00:35.300
I dropped out of school,

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:38.380
took Montessori courses
so I could be an educator.

00:00:38.380 --> 00:00:41.580
Our curriculum is enriched

00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:44.160
and we use everything we can in our power

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:46.810
to develop and encourage
critical thinking.

00:00:46.810 --> 00:00:49.930
Sign language, drama, music.

00:00:49.930 --> 00:00:54.110
We have a cricket club, the
first cricket club in the hood.

00:00:54.110 --> 00:00:57.900
I teach harp, violin, cello, bass, piano.

00:00:57.900 --> 00:01:00.700
We had all these pumpkins
in our little garden

00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:03.870
and that's how the
Sheenway Bakery was born.

00:01:03.870 --> 00:01:07.010
The Chow Wagon was launched
on Juneteenth of this year

00:01:07.010 --> 00:01:09.696
to allow the children
to serve a community.

00:01:09.696 --> 00:01:12.790
- Come get your delicious pumpkin bread.

00:01:12.790 --> 00:01:14.460
- [Dolores] I'm never gonna retire

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:17.360
because as long as I can give,

00:01:17.360 --> 00:01:18.830
I think I'll live.

00:01:18.830 --> 00:01:19.790
It's a good feeling

00:01:19.790 --> 00:01:22.940
when you know that
someone's gonna walk out

00:01:22.940 --> 00:01:25.420
knowing more than they
did when they came in

00:01:25.420 --> 00:01:27.060
and you had a part of it.

00:01:27.060 --> 00:01:30.367
I think that's why I love
children so much, sorry.

00:01:33.320 --> 00:01:37.091
It's like good in the hood.

00:01:37.091 --> 00:01:39.156
(Dolores chuckles)

00:01:39.156 --> 00:01:41.989
(audience cheers)

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:45.810
- Welcome live and in person

00:01:45.810 --> 00:01:48.938
Dolores Sheen, aka Aunt Dolores.

00:01:48.938 --> 00:01:51.729
(audience cheers)

00:01:51.729 --> 00:01:52.562
- Thank you.

00:01:52.562 --> 00:01:53.670
- And I understand you brought

00:01:53.670 --> 00:01:56.090
two special gentlemen here today.

00:01:56.090 --> 00:01:58.092
- Yeah, some good cooks.

00:01:58.092 --> 00:01:59.020
- Oh.

00:01:59.020 --> 00:02:00.670
(Dolores laughs)

00:02:00.670 --> 00:02:03.454
- This is Marcus and that's Jordan.

00:02:03.454 --> 00:02:04.287
(audience cheers)

00:02:04.287 --> 00:02:05.120
- Hi.

00:02:05.120 --> 00:02:06.280
(Dolores chuckles)

00:02:06.280 --> 00:02:09.140
- Marcus, I'd like to ask
what your favorite thing is

00:02:09.140 --> 00:02:11.800
about being a part of this community?

00:02:11.800 --> 00:02:15.900
- It's fun and it's physical education.

00:02:15.900 --> 00:02:19.263
- I love that you summed up
one word that speaks volumes.

00:02:20.350 --> 00:02:22.380
And Jordan, what about for you?

00:02:22.380 --> 00:02:23.925
- I like the food.

00:02:23.925 --> 00:02:25.190
(audience laughs)

00:02:25.190 --> 00:02:29.870
- I think something all people
can relate to and appreciate.

00:02:29.870 --> 00:02:34.780
And you also have Sheenway
sister school in Ghana, Africa.

00:02:34.780 --> 00:02:37.210
Will you please tell
us about that program?

00:02:37.210 --> 00:02:39.560
- Our school here is an underserved area

00:02:39.560 --> 00:02:41.990
of what they call south LA in the hood.

00:02:41.990 --> 00:02:44.260
Our school in Ghana is in the bush.

00:02:44.260 --> 00:02:46.290
It's like an underserved area.

00:02:46.290 --> 00:02:48.540
We were the first
registered private school

00:02:48.540 --> 00:02:49.928
in the Volta region.

00:02:49.928 --> 00:02:52.761
(audience cheers)

00:02:58.069 --> 00:03:00.720
- And you guys brought
some baked goods for us.

00:03:00.720 --> 00:03:04.030
And these are treats from
the Sheenway Bakery, right?

00:03:04.030 --> 00:03:07.520
- Yes, the students own
and operate their bakery

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:11.380
because there's a history
of why we have the bakery.

00:03:11.380 --> 00:03:14.870
And the history stems
from when the community

00:03:14.870 --> 00:03:17.480
and Richard Pryor helped
us get a peace treaty

00:03:17.480 --> 00:03:18.640
with the Bloods and the Crips,

00:03:18.640 --> 00:03:20.990
it's two of the main gang factions.

00:03:20.990 --> 00:03:23.330
And we wanted to say, thank you.

00:03:23.330 --> 00:03:25.930
And that year we had a lot
of pumpkins in our garden.

00:03:25.930 --> 00:03:28.800
So I said, "This time we
make some pumpkin bread."

00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:30.940
And they said, "Let's
give Richard Pryor some."

00:03:30.940 --> 00:03:33.500
So, he loved the pumpkin bread

00:03:33.500 --> 00:03:35.930
and that's how the bakery got started.

00:03:35.930 --> 00:03:37.410
And not only that,

00:03:37.410 --> 00:03:41.130
he came back three times
to talk with the dialogue.

00:03:41.130 --> 00:03:44.650
And that set a different
perspective on the community.

00:03:44.650 --> 00:03:46.930
Like someone knows we're here.

00:03:46.930 --> 00:03:49.050
Someone knows our pain.

00:03:49.050 --> 00:03:52.620
That was more than any money
or anything anybody could give.

00:03:52.620 --> 00:03:55.703
And to this day he is our hero.

00:03:55.703 --> 00:03:57.018
(audience claps)

00:03:57.018 --> 00:03:57.851
To this day.

00:03:57.851 --> 00:03:59.718
(audience claps)

00:03:59.718 --> 00:04:04.718
- The layers of importance and
beauty just keep unfolding.

00:04:05.070 --> 00:04:08.560
And we also have some
special people joining us

00:04:08.560 --> 00:04:10.410
right here in the audience

00:04:10.410 --> 00:04:11.960
who are proud of you

00:04:11.960 --> 00:04:13.830
and what you have done for your community.

00:04:13.830 --> 00:04:17.480
Please welcome Principal Roy Sadakane,

00:04:17.480 --> 00:04:21.930
faculty and alumni from
the Sheenway School, hello!

00:04:21.930 --> 00:04:25.053
(audience cheers)

00:04:25.053 --> 00:04:27.790
- [Roy] All right, three
cheers for Aunt Dolores.

00:04:27.790 --> 00:04:29.267
Hip hip hooray!

00:04:29.267 --> 00:04:31.562
Hip hip hooray!
- Hip hooray!

00:04:31.562 --> 00:04:33.740
Hip hip hooray!
- Hip hip hooray!

00:04:33.740 --> 00:04:35.470
- I love that Principal Roy.

00:04:35.470 --> 00:04:39.440
What is your hope for
Sheenway in the next 50 years?

00:04:39.440 --> 00:04:41.514
- Currently as Aunt Delores had mentioned

00:04:41.514 --> 00:04:44.130
we have a school in Sasekofe, Ghana,

00:04:44.130 --> 00:04:46.270
and we're starting a new
digital infrastructure

00:04:46.270 --> 00:04:49.167
that will connect our Los Angeles school

00:04:49.167 --> 00:04:51.750
to the school in Sasekofe, Ghana.

00:04:51.750 --> 00:04:54.870
- Well, you're gonna need support.

00:04:54.870 --> 00:04:56.090
And you deserve that.

00:04:56.090 --> 00:04:58.250
And to commemorate your 50th anniversary,

00:04:58.250 --> 00:05:02.130
our friends at ConAgra Brands Foundation

00:05:02.130 --> 00:05:04.407
are donating $20,000

00:05:04.407 --> 00:05:08.430
to the Sheenway School
and Educational Center

00:05:08.430 --> 00:05:10.694
in LA, California.

00:05:10.694 --> 00:05:11.527
(audience cheers)
- Oh my God!

00:05:18.039 --> 00:05:20.033
- All right!
- Oh my God!

00:05:20.033 --> 00:05:22.716
- [Drew] Thank you, Dolores.

00:05:22.716 --> 00:05:25.950
Thank you, Marcus and
Jordan, Principal Roy

00:05:25.950 --> 00:05:28.970
and everyone at the Sheenway School

00:05:28.970 --> 00:05:30.730
and Cultural Center in Watts.

00:05:30.730 --> 00:05:33.320
For more information,
you can go on our website

00:05:33.320 --> 00:05:36.010
at thedrewbarrymoreshow.com to support

00:05:36.010 --> 00:05:38.097
this incredible institution.

00:05:38.097 --> 00:05:40.680
(upbeat music)

00:05:42.294 --> 00:05:44.374
♪ Oh oh oh oh ♪

00:05:44.374 --> 00:05:46.180
♪ Oh oh oh oh ♪

